  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (multimodal, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieves 0.586 accuracy, while image-only config_013 (same image encoder, transformer) achieves only 0.260, indicating RNA features are the dominant driver of performance. Question: config_002 uses PCA (a linear projection) for RNA; config_019 swaps in scgpt (a learned, non-linear RNA encoder) while keeping all other settings identical (imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, multiprofile). This isolates whether a more expressive RNA representation can push accuracy beyond 0.586. Why this is best: with 7 experiments remaining, testing the highest-impact single variable (RNA encoder quality, given RNA's clear dominance) around the current best configuration is the most informative exploitation step. A positive result would open a promising direction for further tuning; a null result would confirm PCA is sufficient and redirect effort toward other components (image encoder, fusion, aggregation)."
